###Block: Copies and other lines
Alter Self.COPY=Alter Self (Psionic)		CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Psion,Wilder=2	SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Psychometabolism										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Au																																																		SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.177				DESC:PP:3 Augment: If you spend 4 additional power points, this power's duration increases to (CASTERLEVEL) hours.
Blink.COPY=Blink (Psionic)				CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Psion,Wilder=3	SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Psychoportation										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Vi																																																		SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.178				DESC:PP:5 Augment: If you spend 2 additional power points, this power's duration is (CASTERLEVEL) minutes.
Calm Emotions.COPY=Calm Emotions (Psionic)	CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Psion,Wilder=2	SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Telepathy											TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Me																																																		SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.179				DESC:PP:3
Detect Poison.COPY=Detect Poison (Psionic)	CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Psion,Wilder=1	SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Clairsentience										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Au, Ol							RANGE:20 ft.																																								SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.181				DESC:PP:1
Lighten Load.COPY=Lighten Load (Psionic)		CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Psion,Wilder=3	SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Psychometabolism										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Ol																																							SAVEINFO:None									SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.184	DESC:.CLEAR		DESC:PP:5 This power increases the recipients' carrying capacity for the power's duration (divide the duration by the number of recipients). For purposes of carrying capacity only, treat the power's recipients as though their Strength were increased by 10 points.
Locate Object.COPY=Locate (Psionic)			CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Seer=2		SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Clairsentience										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Vi																																							SAVEINFO:None									SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs		SOURCEPAGE:p.184				DESC:PP:3 This power is not affected by lead or running water. It can be fooled by cloud mind, escape detection, and metamorphosis powers. Augment: You can augment this power in one or more of the following ways. 1. If you spend 2 additional power points, this power can also locate a particular kind of plant. 2. If you spend 4 additional power points, this power can also locate a known or familiar creature. 2. If you spend 1 additional power point, this power's duration is 1 min./level rather than concentration. If you spend 2 additional power points, this power's duration is 10 min./level rather than concentration. If you spend 4 additional power points, this power's duration is 1 hour/level rather than concentration.
Teleport Object.COPY=Teleport Object (Psionic)	CLASSES:.CLEARALL	CLASSES:Nomad=7		SCHOOL:.CLEAR	SCHOOL:Psychoportation										TYPE:Psionic	COMPS:Au, Vi																																																	SOURCELONG:Dark Sun Campaign Setting	SOURCESHORT:dscs								DESC:PP:13 Augment: For every 2 additional power points you spend, the maximum weight increases by 10 lb.

###Block: Descriptions
Accelerate.MOD	DESC:Move faster, +1 on attack rolls, AC, and Reflex saves. When the power ends, you become fatigued for a period equal to the power's duration. PP: Egoist 7, psychic warrior 5. Augment: Augment: You can augment this power in one or more of the following ways. 1. For every 2 additional power points you spend, your bonus on attack rolls and bonus to AC and Reflex saves increase by 1. 2. If you spend 4 additional power points, you can manifest this power as a swift action instead of a standard action. 3. If you spend 5 additional power points, you do not become fatigued at the end of this power's duration.
Antidote Simulation.MOD	DESC:Detoxifies venom in your system. Augment: You can augment this power in one or more of the following ways. 1. If you spend 4 additional power points, this power can affect any willing creature or object of up to (CASTERLEVEL) cubic ft. touched. 2. If you spend 6 additional power points, you can manifest this power as an immediate action, quickly enough to negate initial poison damage.
Aura Reading.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Reveal personal details about the target.
Beacon.MOD	DESC:Creates a ball on light that can become much larger with concentration. Augment: If you spend 4 additional power points, this power's duration increases to (CASTERLEVEL) hours.
Bioflexibilty.MOD	DESC:PP:5 You gain a +10 bonus to Escape Artist checks. Augment: For every 4 additional power points spent, you gain an additional +10 bonus to Escape Artist checks.
Cast Missiles.MOD	DESC:PP:1 You can cast sling stones without a sling, launch arrows without a bow, or launch bolts without a crossbow. The ammunition travels as if it had been fired from a sling, shortbow, or light crossbow (as appropriate) using that weapon's damage, critical, and range. As long as you have the ammunition at hand, you can fire one missile per attack without needing to reload. You can even apply feats from the Point Blank Shot tree to these attacks. Alternatively, you can throw objects you hold as an improvised ranged weapon without suffering the normal -4 penalty. Augment: If you spend 2 additional power points, you may fire ammunition as if using a longbow or heavy crossbow (as appropriate).
Cause Sleep.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Puts a creature of 4 HD oor less into deep slumber. Cause sleep does not affect unconscious creatures, constructs, kreen, or undead creatures. Augment: For every additional power point you spend, this power can affect a target that has Hit Dice equal to 4 + the additional points and its save DC increases by 1.
Complete Healing.MOD	DESC:PP:13 This power allows you to heal yourself completely of all ailments, wounds, and normal diseases. You must place yourself in a trance for 24 hours to accomplish the healing. At the end of this manifesting, you are restored to full hit points, no longer suffer from any temporary ability damage, are no longer exhausted or fatigued, and lose any negative levels you had. You also return to full power points, less the cost of this power. Augment: For every 2 additional power points you spend, the manifesting time is decreased by 2 hours (minimum 2 hours).
Concentrate Water.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Collects water from surrounding area. The amount collected depends on the local terrain type.
Cosmic Awareness.MOD	DESC:PP:17 You perceive all things within the area of effect, including the shallow Gray. The amount of information revealed by this power depends on how long you study a particular area.
Cryokinesis.MOD	DESC:PP:1 You cool a creature or object.
Death Field.MOD	DESC:PP: 5 Sacrifice hitpoints to do an equal amount of negative energy damage to all in range. Undead are healed instead. Augment: For every 4 additional power points you spend, this power's radius increase by 5 feet, and the power's save DC increases by 2.
Deflect Strike.MOD	DESC:PP:1 The target's next melee, missile, or ranged touch attack that round suffers a -20 penalty to the attack roll. Augment: If you spend 6 additional power points, you can manifest this power as an immediate action.
Detect Life.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Reveals living creatures. The amount of information revealed depends on how long you search a particular area.
Detect Moisture.MOD	DESC:PP:5 You detect all creatures greater than Tiny that have moisture, plus any concentration of one gallon or more. The amount of information revealed depends on how long you search a particular area.
Dimensional Screen.MOD	DESC:PP:11 Create a shimmering screen that diverts attacks.
Electroerosion.MOD	DESC:PP:9 You create a ray of energy that shoots forth from your fingertip. You must make a successful ranged touch attack to hit. If the item is so large that it cannot fit within a 3- foot radius, a 3-foot-radius volume of the metal is instantaneously vanishes. Magic or psionic items made of metal are immune to this power. A creature or object that makes a successful Fortitude save is partially affected, taking only 4d6 points of damage. If this damage reduces the creature or object to 0 or fewer hit points, it is entirely destroyed. Augment: For every additional power point you spend, the damage this power deals to a target that fails its saving throw increases by 1d6 points.
Ghost Writing.MOD	DESC:PP:1 You can write messages on blank paper or parchment at a distance. You can form up to five words per round.
Hallucination.MOD	DESC:PP:9 Phantasm cause psychosomatic (nonlethal) damage, at most 9d6. Augment: For every additional power point you spend the maximum amount of nonlethal damage increases by one die (d6). For every extra two dice of potential damage, this power's save DC increases by 1.
Hush.MOD	DESC:You send out a subconscious twinge that causes one or more creatures of 4 Hit Dice or less to be as silent as possible. Augment: For every 2 additional power points you spend, this power's range increases by 5 feet and its save DC increases by 1. In addition, for every additional power point you spend to increase the range and the save DC, this power can affect targets that have Hit Dice equal to 4 + the number of additional points.
Incorporeality.MOD	DESC:PP:13 You become incorporeal for (CASTERLEVEL) rounds. Augment: You can augment this power in one or both of the following ways. 1. For every 2 additional power points you spend, you can affect an additional 25 pounds of objects. 2. For every 2 additional power points you spend, this power can affect an additional target. Any additional target cannot be more than 15 feet from another target of the power.
Magnetize.MOD	DESC:PP:7 You can change the magnetic orientation of a mundane metal object, strongly magnetizing it to all metal objects within 20 feet. The targeted object can be made to attract to or repel all metal objects within the field of influence and is affected according to its size category. Magnetic objects, whether they are being attracted or repelled, move in relation to the target at a rate of 10 feet for each size category difference. Augment: For every 2 additional power points you spend, the weight limit of the target increases by 5 pounds, and the power's save DC increases by 1.
Mass Manipulation.MOD	DESC:PP:5 Alter the weight of a creature or object. The mass can be increased up to 200%% its normal weight or reduced to 25%%. Augment: You can augment this power in one or both of the following ways. 1. For every additional power point you spend, the weight limit of target increases by 5 pounds. 2. If you spend 4 additional power points, you can alter the mass between 10%% and 400%%.
Mindflame.MOD	DESC:PP:13 Kills, paralyzes, weakens, or dazes subjects depending on HD.
Molecular Bonding.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Temporarily glue two surfaces together.
Nerve Manipulation.MOD	DESC:PP:9 Disrupts a creature nervous system, stunning, causing spasms, pains, exhaustian, unconsiousness, disabled, dying. Any of these effects can be neutralized by the neutralize poison spell or the antidote simulation power. You can manifest a weaker effect if you want. Augment: You can augment this power in one or more of the following ways. 1. If you spend 2 additional power points, this power can also affect an animal, fey, giant, magical beast, or monstrous humanoid. 2. If you spend 4 additional power points, this power can also affect an aberration, dragon, elemental, or outsider in addition to the creature types mentioned above. In addition, for every 2 additional power points you spend to achieve any of these effects, this power's save DC increases by 1.
Pheromone Discharge.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Vermin react well to you. Augment: If you spend 4 additional power points, this power's duration increases to 1 hour/level.
Photosynthesis.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Transform light into healing. For every hour you rest on a sunny area for the power duration, you heal 5 hit points. Augment: If you spend 4 additional power points, you satisfy the need of a meal and half of your daily water requirement.
Pocket Dimension.MOD	DESC:PP:9 Create a small storage area in an extradimensional space. Augment: For every 2 additional power points you spend, the storage capacity increases 1 cubic foot.
Poison Simulation.MOD	DESC:PP:Egoist 13, Psychic warrior 11 Coat surface with potent poisons. Poison does 2d6 ability damage (your choice) primary and 2d6 ability damage (your choice) secondary damage.
Psionic Draw.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Instantly draw a weapon.
Psionic Sight.MOD	DESC:PP:5 This power allows you to see psionic auras within 120 feet of you. The effect is similar to that of a detect psionics power, but psionic sight does not require concentration and discerns aura location and strength more quickly. Augment: If you spend 8 additional power points, you automatically know which powers or psionic effects are active upon any individual or object you see.
Psychic Tracking.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Track a creature using Psicraft.
Repugnance.MOD	DESC:PP:7 This power causes a creature or object to become completely repugnant to the target. Unless the target makes a Will save, he will try everything reasonable to destroy it. If this causes the target to something against his alignment, he receives a new saving throw.
Return Missile.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Make one weapon return to you after thrown. Augment: You can augment this power in one or both of the following ways. 1. For every 2 additional power points you spend, this power's range increases by 5 feet. 2. For every additional power point you spend, the weight limit of the weapon increases by 2 pounds.
Sensory Suppression.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Victim loses one sense-sight, hearing, smell.
Sever the Tie.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Disrupt an undead's tie to the Gray, doing 3d8 damage. Undead that are brought to 0 hit points or below by use of this power fall limply and molder into dust (if corporeal), or slowly disperse (if incorporeal). Augment: For every 2 additional powerpoints you spend, this power's damage increases by 1d8.
Shadow Jump.MOD	DESC:PP:7 Jump into shadow to travel rapidly. Augment: You can augment this power in one or both of the following ways. 1. If you spend 2 additional power points, you may also bring one additional willing Medium or smaller creature (carrying gear or objects up to its maximum load). 2. If you spend 6 additional power points, you can manifest this power as a move action.
Share Strength.MOD	DESC:PP:3 Temporarily transfer half of  up to (CASTERLEVEL) Strength to another. Augment: If you spend 6 additional power points, you can manifest this power as a swift action instead of a standard action.
Tattoo Animation.MOD	DESC:PP:1 Animates your tattoos or steals another's. Augment: For each additional 4 power points you spent, you can transfer or steal an additional tattoo.
Trail of Destruction.MOD	DESC:Detects recent defiling.
Truthear.MOD	DESC:PP:5 Receive +20 bonus to Sense Motive checks made to tell whether someone is lying.
Watcher Ward.MOD	DESC:PP:3 You are aware of creature within the warded area. You cannot be caught flatfooted and can always act in the surprise round of combat. If you leave the warded area, this power ends prematurely. Augment: If you spend 3 additional power points you know the exact location of all creatures within the area (although you know where they are this power does not enable you to see hidden or invisible creatures).
Weather Prediction.MOD	DESC:PP:5 Predicts weather for next 24 hours.
Wild Leap.MOD	DESC:PP:1 You are able make a Jump check, catch yourself for a split second and then make a second Jump check. In addition, you receive a +5 competence bonus on Jump checks made in conjunction with this power. Augment: For each additional 4 power points you spend, you gain an additional +5 bonus to the Jump check.
Aging.MOD	DESC:Make subject older.
Create Element.MOD	DESC:Create a small amount of patron element.
Detect Element.MOD	DESC:Detect presence of element.
Bless Element.MOD	DESC:Makes holy element.
Cooling Canopy.MOD	DESC:Summons a cloud to provide shade and prevent dehydration.
Curse Element.MOD	DESC:Makes unholy element.
Heat Lash.MOD	DESC:Creature suffers 1d4+1 damage and is knocked back 5 ft. A successful save reduces the damage by half and prevents the creature from being knocked back.
Return to the Earth.MOD	DESC:Turns dead and undead bodies into dust.
Eye of the Storm.MOD	DESC:Protects 30 ft. radius from effects of storm.
Sand Pit.MOD	DESC: Excavates sand in a 30 ft. wide and 50 ft. deep cylinder.
Surface Walk.MOD	DESC:Subject treads on unstable surfaces as if solid. If the spell is cast underwater or under silt (or while the subjects are partially or wholly submerged in whatever liquid they are in), the subjects are borne toward the surface at 60 feet per round until they can stand on it.
Worm's Breath.MOD	DESC:Subjects can breathe underwater, in silt or earth.
Control Tides.MOD	DESC:Raises, lowers, or parts bodies of water or silt.
Curse of the Black Sands.MOD	DESC:Target leaves black oily footprints.
Elemental Armor.MOD	DESC:Armor or shield gains +(min(5,(CASTERLEVEL-6)/3)) enhancement bonus and special quality depending on patron element. Air; Arrow catching. Earth; Light fortification. Fire; Fire resistance. Magma; Fire resistance. Rain; Electricity resistance. Silt; Acid resistance. Sun; Blinding. Water; Cold resistance. You become proficient in the armor this spell is cast upon for the duration of the spell. Creatures other than you wearing the armor enjoy no benefits from the spell's effects. This spell's subtype is the same as the type of energy you cast.
Elemental Weapon.MOD	DESC:Weapon gains +(min(5,(CASTERLEVEL-6)/3)) enhancement bonus and special quality depending on patron element. If the weapon is a double-weapon, only one end is affected. Air; Throwing. Earth; Mighty cleaving. Fire; Flaming. Magma; Flaming. Rain; Shock. Silt; Keen. Sun; Spell storing. Water; Frost. You become proficient with the weapon this is spell is cast upon for the duration of the spell. Creatures other than you wielding the weapon enjoy no benefits from the spell's effects. This spell's subtype is the same as the type of energy you cast.
Sand Spray.MOD	DESC:Sprays sand or silt as an area attack. Creatures within the area are blinded for 1d6 minutes and take piercing damage: 2d6 nonlethal and 2d6 lethal. A successful Reflex save halves the damage and blinds a creature for only one round. Note that this spell does not create the tiny shards; sand or silt must be within range for this spell to take effect.
Cleansing Flame.MOD	DESC:Bolt of flame that does (min(10,CASTERLEVEL))d6 fire damage. This spell can only affect defilers, templars whose sorcerer-kings are defilers, creatures with the defiled template, creatures with the evil subtype, and undead. The bolt strikes unerringly, even if the target is in melee combat or has less than total cover or total concealment. Specific parts of a creature can't be singled out. A creature killed by this spell has its remains utterly consumed (but not its equipment and possessions). The only way to restore life to a creature that was killed in this way is to use wish, true resurrection, reality revision, or miracle.
Elemental Strike.MOD	DESC:Smites foes with (min(15,CASTERLEVEL))d6 of divine and elemental energy. The type of energy damage, as well as the energy descriptor of the spell, is chosen at the time of casting. Clerics must choose the energy type that corresponds to their patron element.
Ragestorm.MOD	DESC:Summons a storm with high winds, hail, and lightning. The storm inflicts 4d8 points of damage to anyone within its radius on a failed save due to high winds, dangerous hail, and electrical discharges. A creature that fails its saving throw can't run out of the area of effect, for they carry the storm with them wherever they go.
Rangeblade.MOD	DESC:The wielder of the weapon can strike opponents at a distance, just as if he was standing directly next to them. The maximum range for attacks with the rangeblade is (((CASTERLEVEL/2)+1)*5) ft. A rangeblade threatens no area and cannot provide a flanking bonus. This spell does not grant the wielder proficiency in the weapon.
Braxatskin.MOD	DESC:Your skin hardens, granting +5 enhancment to natural armor, -2 Dex penalty, additional 20%% arcane spell failure, grow +5 armor spikes (also granting proficiency) and grants DR 10/metal.
Rejuvenate.MOD	DESC:Increase the fertility of the land.
Elemental Chariot.MOD	DESC:This spell imbues a masterwork chariot with elemental magic. The caster must provide a crodlu and a driver with the Handle Animal skill (though the caster may be the driver). The crew (crodlu, driver, and passengers) all gain damage reduction 10/magic against ranged weapons. All ranged weapons fired from the chariot gain a +4 enhancement bonus and deal an additional 5 points of elemental damage based on the element imbued. Clerics must choose the energy type that corresponds their patron element. The chariot may make horizontal "jumps" using the driver's Handle Animal skill in lieu of a Jump roll (but the chariot's ground speed still affects the check). Air; Sonic. Earth; Acid. Fire; Fire. Magma; Fire. Rain; Electricity. Silt; Acid. Sun; Fire. Water; Cold. This spell's subtype is the same as the type of energy you cast.
Sands of Time.MOD	DESC:Reverses or accelerates aging of a non-living object depending on casterlevel (see table).
Unliving Identity.MOD	DESC:Transforms a zombie into a thinking zombie by recalling it's consciousness from the Gray. This spell restores personality, memory, identity, skills, class levels-everything but life. If the creature is unwilling to return, it can make a Will save using its save bonus from life (not that of the target zombie). The spirit's spell resistance, if any, also applies.
Elemental Storm.MOD	DESC:Deals (min(20,CASTERLEVEL))d6 energy damage to all creatures in the target area except natural vegetation, ground cover, and plant creatures you wish to exclude. The type of energy damage, as well as the energy descriptor of the spell, is chosen at the time of casting. Clerics must choose the energy type that corresponds to their patron element.
Elemental Chariot (Greater).MOD	DESC:This spell functions as elemental chariot, except as noted above and as follows. The spell provides the following additional benefits depending on the element imbued. Air; The chariot and crodlu gain a fly speed equal to the crodlu's base land speed (poor maneuverability). Earth; The chariot and crodlu can burrow through earth or solid rock at the crodlu's base land speed. The chariot leaves no tunnel. Fire; You can concentrate to make the chariot leave a wall of fire in its wake (on one edge of each square it leaves). This fire acts as the spell, except that it emits heat at half range on both sides and lasts (CASTERLEVEL) rounds. The chariot cannot leave a wake two rounds in a row. Magma; You can concentrate to make the chariot leave molten lava in its wake (on one edge of each square it leaves) that takes (CASTERLEVEL) rounds to cool. Heat rising from the lava has the same effect as a wall of fire, as the spell, except it emits heat at half range on both sides. The chariot cannot leave a wake two rounds in a row. Silt; You can concentrate to make the chariot leave a wake of cloudkill. This wake acts as the spell, except that it only fills each square the chariot leaves, the cloud doesn't move, and it lasts (CASTERLEVEL) rounds. The chariot cannot leave a wake two rounds in a row. Sun; The chariot shines with such dazzling brightness that anyone within 60 feet that looks directly at the chariot must make a Fortitude save or be blinded for 1d4 rounds. Those who succeed at the save are instead dazzled for the same duration. Water or Rain; The chariot, crodlu, and crew all enjoy the benefits of the displacement spell, and the chariot may pass underwater for up to (CASTERLEVEL) rounds at a time without the animals or passengers needing air. The chariot and crodlu have a swim speed equal to the crodlu's base land speed. This spell's subtype is the same as the type of energy you cast.
Heartseeker.MOD	DESC:When the weapon damages a creature, the wooden shaft of the weapon begins to sprout as if growing. The roots and branches seek out vital organs as a source of nutrients. If the creature fails a Fortitude save, the vines burst through the victim's vital organs, killing him instantly. If the save is successful, the creature manages to pull the weapon out but takes 10d8 points of damage. The weapon is destroyed after being used. Creatures immune to critical hits automatically make their Fortitude save.
Sand Trap.MOD	DESC:You trap an area of sand. You must designate a 30-foot radius "trigger area" somewhere within the larger area. When a creature sets foot inside the trigger area, the trap is sprung, and all of the entrapped area is affected with one of the following effects (your choice): Drum Sand: Every footstep taken within the entrapped area of sand is amplified so loudly that it can be heard for miles, typically attracting predators. Sand Spikes: Treat the entire entrapped area as though affected by spike stones. Slip Sand: The entire area of sand becomes difficult to travel. Treat the area as if affected by the grease spell.
Sand Flow.MOD	DESC:You shift the location of sand dunes.
Glass Storm.MOD	DESC:Creates a whirlwind of broken glass. creatures and unattended objects take 2d8 points of damage per round until they leave the area. All unprotected flames in the spell's area are extinguished. Note that this spell does not create the tiny shards; sand or silt must be within range for this spell to take effect.
Molten.MOD	DESC:Melt sand into glass, or rock into magma. Damage increases each round. Cooldown takes hours.
Fissure.MOD	DESC:Opens a volcanic fissure in natural stone.
Clues of Ash.MOD	DESC:You receive a vision of an item's destruction. The vision begins from the time the object was destroyed or killed, going backward in time up to (CASTERLEVEL) minutes. You can also tell whether the object was destroyed by defiler destruction or not. If vegetation destroyed by defiling is tested, you can make a Spellcraft check (DC 15 + spell level) to determine the school of magic cast.
Fire Track.MOD	DESC:Fiery spark follows tracks.
Watch Fire.MOD	DESC:You use a small fire to scry through other fires within range. You know how many fires burn within range and the approximate location of each. Once per minute, you may choose one of these fires and peer out of it as if you were actually within the flames. Anyone watching the fire sees a dark face within but can only dispel the visage by extinguishing the flame or casting some form of protection from scrying. You may communicate through the flames but cannot cast spells or use other abilities. If your flame is put out, then the spell ends prematurely.
Confessor's Flame.MOD	DESC:Uses threat of flame to extract confession.
Spirit of Flame.MOD	DESC:You use a small fire to scry through other fires within range. You know how many fires burn within range and the approximate location of each. Once per minute, you may choose one of these fires and peer out of it as if you were actually within the flames. Anyone watching the fire sees a dark face within but can only dispel the visage by extinguishing the flame or casting some form of protection from scrying. You may communicate through the flames, and cast spells as if you were actually within the flames. Spells cast through the fire cannot require somatic components. Creatures can target you through the fire with light- and sonic-based attacks, and with mind-affecting effects. In addition, you can walk into a fire and greater teleport to any other fire up to the limit of your range. If the original fire that you used to scry is put out, you can still use other fires within range.
Cerulean Hail.MOD	DESC:A hailstorm appears and does (min(15,CASTERLEVEL))d6 damage, half bludgeoning, half cold (reflex save for half) and causes creatures with less than 10 HD who come within 60 feet and fail a Will save to become panicked for 1d4 rounds.
Gray Beckoning.MOD	DESC:Summons gray zombies
Gray Rift.MOD	DESC:This spell tears and holds open a rift between Athas and the Gray. The rift itself is a two-dimensional, diamond-shaped plane 30 feet high and 15 feet wide in the middle. Any creature that touches the rift is affected as if you cast harm on it. A character that attempts to dispel the rift and fails is also subjected to harm. Once pe  round as a move action, you can move the rift 30 feet in any direction within range. If you cease concentration or are slain, the rift lingers for 1d6 rounds without moving and then dissipates. All undead creatures within range gain a +4 profane bonus to Strength, 3 bonus hit points per hit die, and fast healing 1.
Vampiric Youthfulness.MOD	DESC:This spell makes you younger at the expense of another creature. The victim must have Hit Dice equal or greater than your character level and must be at full hit points when you cast the spell. The caster and the victim must be in continuous contact throughout the casting of this spell; any interruption negates the spell. At the completion of this spell, the victim ages ten years while you become one year younger. Outsiders and plants are immune to this spell.
Acid Rain.MOD	DESC:Conjures an acidic shower doing 4d4 acid damage each round.
Curse of the Choking Sands.MOD	DESC:Victim's touch turns water to sand.
Coat of Mists.MOD	DESC:Coalesces a magical mist about the subject's body. This grants fire resistance 5, protection against hot water as endure elements, and grants concealment (20%% miss chance).
Shining Sands.MOD	DESC:This spell can only be cast outside, in sand, during the daytime. It can be cast one of two ways. Reflected Outward; All creatures outside the area but within 60 feet of its center are blinded for 1 round unless they make a Fortitude save. A creature must save each round it remains in the area. Reflected Inward; All creatures within the area are blinded unless they make a Fortitude save, but creatures outside the area can look into it with no risk of being blinded.
Surface Tension.MOD	DESC:Affected water acquires rubbery surface.
Lungs of Water.MOD	DESC:Conjures water inside victim's lungs.
Water Trap.MOD	DESC:Body of water becomes death trap. When a creature of Large size or smaller (but no larger than the body of water) touches the pool, oasis, or watering hole altered by this spell, it must make an immediate Reflex saving throw. Failure indicates that the victim is instantly pulled under the surface and trapped. Creatures pulled under by this spell will find that the surface of the water now has a tough, rubbery consistency that makes escape very difficult. Treat the water's surface as if affected by the surface tension spell.
Drown on Dry Land.MOD	DESC:Targets can only breathe water.
Whirlpool of Doom.MOD	DESC:You stir the ground into a whirlpool of rock and earth.
Flash Flood.MOD	DESC:Conjures a flood.
Flame Harvest.MOD	DESC:Creates a conditioned fire trap doing 8d8 fire damage when triggered.
Conflagration.MOD	DESC:Creatures caught in the blast suffer 10d6 points of fire damage (no save) and automatically catch on fire (DMG 303). Creatures on fire suffer 2d6 points of fire damage for each round. Unlike mundane fire, this fire cannot be put out by normal means. Spraying a creature caught on fire by this spell with water or sand only creates a billowing cloud of steam or hot dust out to 20 ft. from the target; instead of the normal damage, creatures within the cloud suffer 5d6 points of fire damage and are sickened for one round. Complete immersion in a large amount of water, or burial beneath the sand, reduces damage to 1d6 point per round for both the creature on fire and those within 20 ft. A successful dispel magic or quench spell puts out the fire.
Sandstone.MOD	DESC:Your touch packs sand into sandstone
Legendary Stonecraft.MOD	DESC:Stretches time with respect to stonecraft labor.
Storm Legion.MOD	DESC:Transports willing creatures via a natural storm.
Channel Stench.MOD	DESC:All breathing creatures within the cone must make a Fortitude save. Those who fail become nauseated for 1d6 rounds. Those who succeed instead become sickened for 1d6 rounds. Creatures with 5 or more Hit Dice are immune to this effect.
Breeze Lore.MOD	DESC:Gives you temporary scent ability. See text for details.
Poisoned Gale.MOD	DESC:This spell resembles gust of wind, except that the range is shorter and the wind is filled with inhaled poison. You choose the ability score you would like the poison to damage. Poison gale creates a poison that deals 2d8 points of temporary ability damage as primary and secondary damage. The exception is Constitution, which is damaged 1d8 points. The ability score damaged does not have to be the same for the primary and secondary damage.
Wind Trap.MOD	DESC:Prepare a magical wind trap to spring on specified conditions. When the conditions that you specify are met, the trap discharges, creating a cloud of fumes 30 feet high. You can designate these fumes to duplicate stinking cloud, cloudkill, acid fog, or incendiary cloud, or you can use this cloud to distribute a contact or inhaled poison used as a material component.
Clear Water.MOD	DESC:You make water twice as effective at quenching thirst and nourishing plant life.
Pact of Water.MOD	DESC:Seal a pledge between willing creatures.
Sweet Water.MOD	DESC:Enhances water with life-preserving properties. (can breathe normally in this water, drink to gain +4 resistance bonus on Save vs poison, heal 1d8 hit points)
Awaken Water Spirits.MOD	DESC:Gives sentience to a body of natural water.
Waters of Life.MOD	DESC:Absorb another creature's ailments, up to and including death!
Waterways.MOD	DESC:Use water sources as conduit for teleportations for the duration of the spell.
Oil Spray.MOD	DESC:A fountain of flammable oil gushes from the ground.
Repel Metal or Wood.MOD	DESC:Pushes away metal or wooden objects.
Magma Tunnel.MOD	DESC:Tunnels through solid rock.
Swarm of Anguish.MOD	DESC:Transforms you into a swarm of agony beetles.
Water Shock.MOD	DESC:This spell entraps a small body of water (ranging from 1 pint to 100 gallons) with an electric charge. The first creature to touch the water receives a shock that inflicts (min(5,CASTERLEVEL/2))d6 points of electricity damage. The water instantly evaporates when the spell discharges.
Liquid Lightning.MOD	DESC:This spell entraps a small body of water (ranging from 1 pint to 100 gallons) with an electric charge. An effect similar to chain lightning strikes the first creature to touch the water, with secondary bolts striking all creatures within 60 feet. The creature that triggers the trap suffers (min(20,CASTERLEVEL))d6 points of electricity damage and is paralyzed for 1d6 minutes if it fails its Fortitude save. Secondary targets receive half damage and are not paralyzed.
Water Light.MOD	DESC:With the exception of you and everything that you are carrying, all living creatures and objects that contain more than one gallon of water glow as if affected by a light spell. Once per round, as a free action, you may cause an affected creature or object to emit lightning. The affected creature or object takes 5d8 points of electricity damage. Creatures within 10 feet of the target also take 5d8 points of electricity damage but may make a Reflex save for half damage.
Blindscorch.MOD	DESC:Fire burns the face of one opponent, doing (min(10,CASTERLEVEL))d4 damage and permanently blinding. Fortitude save halves damage and negates blindness.
Blazing Wreath.MOD	DESC:Shrouds you in elemental flame, doing 2d8 fire damage to creatures within 10 ft. Provides DR 15/magic, immunity to fire. You leave a wall of fire in your wake (2d6+(min(20,CASTERLEVEL)) fire damage when passing through). Provides illumination as a daylight spell.
Death Whip.MOD	DESC:Enhances a whip to deal 1d2 temporary strength damage.
Air Lens.MOD	DESC:Directs intensified sunlight at foes within range doing 2d6+(CASTERLEVEL) damage.
Defiler Scent.MOD	DESC:Smells the presence or absence of defilers.
Nurturing Seeds.MOD	DESC:Makes 10 seeds or cuttings hardy and easy to transplant.
Black Cairn.MOD	DESC:Locates a corpse nearby.
Plant Renewal.MOD	DESC:Brings one plant back from near destruction.
Proof Against Undeath.MOD	DESC:Prevents dead subject from being raised as undead.
Boneharden.MOD	DESC:Hardens bone, making bone weapons stronger (ignore normal penalties) or impairing living beings (-4 DEX).
Conservation.MOD	DESC:If a defiler tries to use land that is under a conservation spell to power his spells, he must make a Will save or be unable to use the land at all. Even if he succeeds, the land is considered as barren terrain for the purposes of determining the spell's DC and level check modifier. The area of ash the defiler actually creates when tapping land under a conservation spell is half that of normal. A second attempt to pull power from the same area for the duration of the spell fails completely, regardless of any success achieved the first time.
Echo of the Lirr.MOD	DESC:Creatures caught in the cone of sound you emit must make a successful Will save or be stunned for 1d3 rounds. Creatures that cannot hear are not stunned.
Sting of the Gold Scorpion.MOD	DESC:Enlivens scorpion barb to strike with poison of real scorpion once. Primary damage 1d6 temporary Strength damage. Secondary damage 1d4 temporary Strength damage.
Boneclaw's Cut.MOD	DESC:Deals (min(5,CASTERLEVEL/4)) cuts that do 2 damage each. Each cut continues to cause 2 bleeding damage for 10 rounds (which can be stopped with a DC 15 Heal check or cure spell).
Claws of the Tembo.MOD	DESC:You grow vicious claws similar to those of a tembo. You may make two claw attacks per round, each dealing 1d6 (1d8 if you are Large, or 1d4 if you are Small) points of damage plus your Strength modifier. Like the dreaded tembo, your claws can drain a victim's life force and transfer it to you. Every time you hit with a claw, the creature struck must make a Fortitude save. If it fails, it takes an additional 1d4 points of damage, and you heal that many hit points. If the transferred hit points bring your total above your normal maximum, the additional hit points are temporary hit points. You are unable to cast spells with somatic components while this spell is in effect.
Clear-river.MOD	DESC:This spell functions like gust of wind; except that the effect is force-based and that the creature sizes affected by the spell are increased by one size category (i.e. Large creatures are unable to move forward against the force of the blast). The roaring blast is sufficient to tear objects from unsuspecting hands within the area of effect. (A Reflex save allows a creature to maintain its grasp on an object.) Arrows, bolts, and spears are deflected away and miss. (A giant-thrown boulder, a siege engine projectile, and other massive ranged weapons are not affected.) Incorporeal creatures, gases, most gaseous breath weapons, and creatures in gaseous form are shunted away from the area of the blast.
Zombie Berry.MOD	DESC:Casting zombie berry on a handful of berries from a zombie plant temporarily alters them so that instead of becoming enslaved by the zombie plant, the one who consumes such a berry becomes your loyal servant instead. You can always tell which berries you have affected. Any humanoid eating one of the berries must succeed at a Will save or be affected as by the charm person spell (this is a mind-affecting effect).
Klar's Heart.MOD	DESC:You magically enhance the combat ability of all living creatures, allies and enemies alike, within 20 feet (including you). Subjects of the spell receive a +4 enhancement bonus to Strength and +(CASTERLEVEL/2)d4 temporary hit points.
Conversion.MOD	DESC:Removes burden of acts of defiling from a wizard.
Groundflame.MOD	DESC:A highly corrosive mist deals (min(15,CASTERLEVEL))d6 points of acid damage to each creature in the area.
Skyfire.MOD	DESC:This spell functions like meteor swarm, except that you create three egg-sized spheres that inflict 1d6 points of bludgeoning damage (no save), and 3d6 points of fire damage in a 5-ft.-radius spread.
Allegiance of the Land.MOD	DESC:Grants +5 enhancement bonus to AC, (CASTERLEVEL) temporary hit points, and you may ignore 15 points of energy damage per round.
Create Oasis.MOD	DESC:Conjures a temporary oasis.
Sirocco.MOD	DESC:You conjure a legendary, uncontrolled desert wind. Each round of exposure to the storm inflicts 2d8 points of piercing and bludgeoning damage to all creatures and objects in the area. Creatures with total cover take no damage.
Wild Lands.MOD	DESC:Attract wild creatures to an area.
Footsteps of the Quarry.MOD	DESC:Track a specific creature or person. You are treated as having the Track feat and receive a +2  bonus on Survival checks to follow tracks of you quarry. If the quarry travels in a way other than on land, the trail ceases. Only after the quarry has resumed traveling by land does the trail continue. This spell works against trackless step or other forms of concealing tracks.
Hand of the Sorcerer-king.MOD	DESC:You receive a +2 sacred or profane bonus to all saving throws against spells and spell-like abilities, depending on the alignment of your sorcerer-king.
Battlefield Healing.MOD	DESC:Stabilizes (CASTERLEVEL) creatures.
Dedication.MOD	DESC:Allows target to avoid sleep, consume half food and water, and +1 to attack, damage, saves, ability, and skill checks while pursuing a specified task.
Image of the Sorcerer-King.MOD	DESC:A touched creature must succeed on a Will save or become frightened. On a successful save the target is shaken for one round. Creatures with more than 10 Hit Dice are unaffected by the spell.
Fool's Feast.MOD	DESC:You turn an ordinary banquet into a nourishing feast with the same 12-hour blessing effect as the food and drink provided by the heroes' feast spell. In addition, you receive a +4 circumstance bonus to interaction checks (such as Bluff, Diplomacy, Intimidate, and Sense Motive) when dealing with those who have consumed the feast. This spell can only be cast on a sufficient supply of clean, unpoisoned, edible food and wine. This spell enhances the food's appearance, flavor, and texture to resemble the ambrosia and the sumptuous food available through heroes' feast.
Mage Seeker.MOD	DESC:Locate nearby wizard.
Wrath of the Sorcerer-king.MOD	DESC:You instantly know what crimes the creatures committed, when, and under what circumstances. There is no save to avoid the divination. If you have one of the following spells available, you may immediately cast it at a creature within the area. Casting the spell is a free action, like casting a quickened spell, and it counts toward the normal limit of one quickened spell per round. You may choose from cause fear, command, dispel magic, and hold person. The target can make a Will save to avoid the effect (except for dispel magic), and the spell functions normally in all other ways.
Wisdom of the Sorcerer-king.MOD	DESC:You may apply one of the following metamagic feats to a spell of 4th level or lower you cast this turn: Empower Spell, Enlarge Spell, Extend Spell, Maximize Spell, Silent Spell, or Still Spell.
Crusade.MOD	DESC:Allies receive +4 morale bonus to attack rolls, damage rolls, and saving throws, 2d8 temporary hit points, and immunity to fear effects.
Slave Scent.MOD	DESC:Divines target's social class.
Illusory Talent.MOD	DESC:You make it seem as though you and a single other willing person possess talent in performance ability. You both receive a +10 bonus on Perform checks. This spell does not actually impart any skill or learning; you do not perform any better than you could before, but it appears to observers that you do. However, simply watching or listening to the performance counts as "interaction", and observers may make a Will save to notice the illusion. Otherwise, the performance appears flawless.
Wakefulness.MOD	DESC:The subject of this spell cannot naturally fall asleep. When this spell ends, the subject becomes exhausted. Another wakefulness cast before the previous expires allows the subject to stave off exhaustion, but the subject must afterwards get eight hours of sleep for each casting to remove exhaustion or fatigue. This spell counters, and is countered by, spells that induce magical slumber (such as sleep).
Cerulean Shock.MOD	DESC:Imbue target with harmful static electricity. If the target leaves its occupied square it takes (2*(CASTERLEVEL/4)+2)d6 electricity damage. If the affected creature touches someone or something before the spell is discharged, both the target and whatever it touched receives the damage.
Magic Trick.MOD	DESC:Conceal your spellcasting. You receive a +10 circumstance bonus on resisted Bluff checks made to disguise spellcasting while the spell is in effect.
Gloomcloud.MOD	DESC:Make one creature despair.
Ghostfire.MOD	DESC:Kills (min(40,2*CASTERLEVEL)) HD of creatures. No creature of than 5 HD can be affected.
Touch the Black.MOD	DESC:Cold deals (min(15,CASTERLEVEL))d6 damage per level, 40-ft. radius. All within the cube take a -2 penalty on attack rolls, saving throws, skill checks, and ability checks for the next 1d4+1 rounds whether they succeed or not.
Scapegoat.MOD	DESC:This spell causes all creatures within 20 feet of the target to believe he is to blame for all troubles or difficulties they have. All creatures in the area become hostile towards the target. Affected creatures with Intelligence 3 or greater are allowed to make a Will save to come to their senses.
Quietstorm.MOD	DESC:Ranged touch attacks deal 8d6 sonic damage each.
Sparkrain.MOD	DESC:Bolt dispels all defensive force effects on primary target and all first level defensive force effects in a 20-ft. radius.
Sandflow.MOD	DESC:You shift the location of sand dunes.
Banish Tyr-Storm.MOD	DESC:Repel a Tyr-Storm.
Summon Tyr-Storm.MOD	DESC:Call a powerful Tyrstorm which lasts 2d10 minutes and does 2d8 damage per round. A Tyr-storm is a violent tempest and can't be used to bring water. This spell does not imbue you with the ability to control the Tyr-storm.
Shroud of Darkness.MOD	DESC:You imbue an ordinary cloak with magical power. While wearing it, you gain damage reduction 5/magic, darkvision out to 60 feet and a deflection bonus to AC equal to your Charisma bonus. The cloak also allows you to enter and exit the Black as a standard action. If you enter an area without any source of illumination, the spell ends.
Protection from Time.MOD	DESC:This spell makes a living creature immune to natural, magical, and psionic aging. This spell continues on beyond the creature's death, and time limits for spells like speak with dead or raise dead do not count the time that protection from time is in effect. This spell can be cast on a dead creature. The target moves through time at the same rate as other beings. A living subject must still eat, drink and rest as usual; it simply does not age. This spell does not affect the duration of other spells.
Tempest.MOD	DESC:Create an obliterating storm. Any living creatures in the designated area must make a Reflex save or be completely obliterated.
Pact of Darkness.MOD	DESC:Exchange services with a shadow giant.
Firewater.MOD	DESC:You give water the intoxicating properties of brewed spirits, such as wine or broy. A cup of this water acts as a poison (the Fortitude save DC is equal save DC this spell would have) that deals no initial damage, and 1 point of Wisdom damage and 1 point of Dexterity damage, as secondary damage. Detect poison positively detects firewater, but the water tastes and smells like normal water.

###Block: Other modifications
Create Water.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1
Bless Water.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1
Curse Water.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1
Water Breathing.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1,Ranger=1
Water Walk.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1,Druid=1,Ranger=1
Control Water.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1,Druid=1,Wizard=1
Flame Strike.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1,Druid=1
Wall of Stone.MOD	PREDOMAIN:1,Earthen Embrace
Fire Storm.MOD	!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1,Druid=1
